%% section: Connection pooling
%% caption: Why the pool size matters
flowchart TB
    APP["App instances × threads"] --> POOL["Connection pool"]
    POOL --> PG["Postgres — one backend process per connection"]
    PG --> MEM["Each backend costs memory and a scheduler slot"]
    MEM --> THRASH["Too many: context switching, lock contention, throughput falls"]
    POOL --> SMALL["Too few: queueing at the pool, latency climbs"]
    POOL --> RIGHT["Right size ≈ cores × 2 + effective spindles"]
    PGB["PgBouncer — transaction pooling"] -.-> PG
    PGB --> NOTE["Multiplexes many clients onto few backends"]
    NOTE --> CAVEAT["Breaks session state: prepared statements, advisory locks, temp tables"]
